_Note added in proof._ - The equation \\beta=2\\alpha/(\\alpha-2) is only valid for \\beta<4. As shown in Table 1 this results, however, in values of \\beta larger than 4. For turbulence spectra with \\beta>4, a relationship \\beta=6-8/\\alpha is valid (Cordes et al., 1986, ApJ, 310, 737; Romani et al., 1986, MNRAS, 220, 19). Applying this to \\alpha listed in Table 1 results however in values \\beta<4. We conclude again that our results are not consistent with standard theory. We also note that a scatter broadening function s(t)=1/\\sqrt{t}\\,\\exp(-t/\\tau_{\\rm sc}), which is a conceivable alternative shape in the limit of one-dimensional scatterers that might pertain to situations with large scattering (Cordes 2001, private communication), does not appropriately describe our scattered profiles, in contrast to s(t) used in the Letter.